# en_wordlist.combined.gz

The English word list from the Android Open Source Project's LatinIME keyboard.

- Source: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/inputmethods/LatinIME/+/refs/heads/main/dictionaries/en_wordlist.combined.gz
- Retrieved: 2026-08-19
- Header: `dictionary=main:en,locale=en,description=English,date=1414726273,version=54`
- Entries: 165,544 words, each with a 0-255 frequency and its own casing
- Licence: Apache License 2.0, Copyright (C) The Android Open Source Project

The list is vendored rather than downloaded at build time so
`engine/tools/gen-wordrank.py` reproduces `WordRank.swift` offline.

The 2014 date is a known limit: the list has `iPhone` and `Mateo`, and it does
not have `Jaxon` or `Malia`.

# count_2w.txt.gz

Peter Norvig's two-word counts, the quarter-million most frequent lowercase
bigrams of the Google Web Trillion Word Corpus.

- Source: https://norvig.com/ngrams/count_2w.txt
- Retrieved: 2026-09-11
- Entries: 286,358 bigrams with counts, none below 100,000. Contractions are
  split into two tokens ("don t"), so no pair contains an apostrophe
- Provenance, as stated at https://norvig.com/ngrams/: "Data files are derived
  from the Google Web Trillion Word Corpus, as described by Thorsten Brants and
  Alex Franz, and distributed by the Linguistic Data Consortium." Norvig
  publishes the count files openly on that page; the code beside them is MIT.

The file is vendored so `engine/tools/gen-wordpairs.py` reproduces
`WordPairs.swift` offline. Web text is the known limit: the counts hold
"bad ass" at 204,647 and never saw a text message.
